From f4afdbd77bc2137811d0405088a1dd711f76e598 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Hodges <git@danielhodges.dev>
Date: Sat, 4 Apr 2026 23:19:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] sched/minlat: Improve LLC balancing, SMT awareness, and
 saturation performance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Comprehensive improvements to the MINLAT scheduling class addressing
LLC-aware task placement, SMT-aware CPU selection, and responsiveness
under saturation. Benchmarked with schbench across 60-100% load against
EEVDF and scx_lavd.

LLC stickiness and migration:
- Waive LLC stickiness when source LLC has no idle cores (cache warmth
  is illusory under full contention)
- Skip LLC recency penalty in migration scoring when source LLC is
  fully busy
- Bypass cache-hot check for idle-pull destinations (any work beats
  idle)
- Increase idle-pull scan depth from 4 to 8 when system is overloaded

SMT-aware task placement:
- Add minlat_smt_sibling_same_tgid() helper to check if an SMT
  sibling runs a task from the same thread group
- Two-phase wakeup scan: fast in-LLC scan (prev_cpu start, cache-
  local), then targeted randomized off-LLC scan only when in-LLC has
  no idle cores
- When LLC cores are saturated (>50% busy), prefer off-LLC idle cores
  over in-LLC SMT siblings — a dedicated physical core beats shared
  execution resources regardless of tgid
- Skip prev_cpu fast path when it's an SMT sibling of a busy core
  and the LLC is core-saturated — fall through to find idle cores

Fork balancing:
- When local LLC is core-saturated, defer to pick-2 LLC comparison
  instead of returning first idle local CPU — spreads forked threads
  across LLCs from initial placement

Saturation improvements:
- Adaptive scheduling period: scale latency target with queue depth
  (minlat_sched_period) matching CFS's __sched_period behavior
- Cap periodic balance interval at 4x base when overloaded CPUs exist
  (vs default 32x busy_factor)
- Halve PELT imbalance threshold when system is overloaded
- Disable preempt resist when CPU has 3+ tasks or when overloaded
  with idle CPUs available
- Halve wakeup preemption threshold at 3+ effective tasks and bypass
  preempt resist
- Active balance push to underloaded CPUs (not just idle) when queue
  depth reaches 3+

Newidle balance:
- Fast LLC-local newidle pull: lightweight scan on every transition
  to idle, grabs nearest overloaded CPU without full topology walk
- Cross-LLC newidle probe: samples 1-2 random off-LLC CPUs when
  LLC-local scan finds nothing
- Kick idle CPUs on enqueue: when a CPU transitions to overloaded,
  send resched IPI to nearest idle LLC-local CPU for immediate pull

Preempt resist:
- Add tunable preempt_resist_ns (debugfs) with 2ms default
- Track last_preempt_ts per entity for resist window
- Disable resist under contention (3+ tasks) or when idle CPUs exist
  with local overload

Results at 60% load (20 threads / 32 CPUs) vs EEVDF:
  p50 request: 3668us vs 3700us (matched, was 6840us before)
  p99 wakeup:  11us vs 44us (4x better)
  p99.9 wakeup: 40us vs 1966us (49x better)
  RPS: 4115 vs 4175 (98.5% of EEVDF, was 86% before)

Results at 100% load (32 threads / 32 CPUs) vs EEVDF:
  p99 wakeup:  791us vs 1998us (2.5x better)
  p99.9 request: 19808us vs 19424us (matched)
  RPS: 4203 vs 4242 (99% of EEVDF)

Signed-off-by: Daniel Hodges <git@danielhodges.dev>
